Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, firefox | chromium | chromium-browser
Homepage: https://github.com/tpluharik/tuxdisplay
Description: use an iPad as a GNOME Wayland monitor over USB
 TuxDisplay creates a real extended monitor in GNOME Wayland and streams it
 directly to the OpenDisplay iPad app over a normal USB cable. No IP network,
 Internet connection, or Personal Hotspot is required. An authenticated browser
 client remains available on private networks. Other desktop sessions use an
 isolated X11 workspace rather than extending the current desktop.
